  "current_evidence_state": "The supplied-model, local-model, annotation-reference, detection-error, reflected-anchor and proposal-stage results remain unchanged. The adapted single-view control is now explicit: 566/583 pairs within five pixels and 582/583 within ten pixels, compared with 569/583 and 583/583 after two-view averaging. The 18 reviewed-reference misses remain partitioned into 12 confidence-gated cases, three native-NMS losses and three without decoded IoU at least 0.50; these are stage observations, not demonstrated learning causes. Both prepared paired training comparisons await results. The expanded report explains method inputs and operations, matching versus suppression, partial-front denominators, and the specific contribution and limits of 15 external references. Intended robotic-arm localization remains separate from untested arm control and integration. No augmentation-audit result or model promotion is claimed in this document update.",
